Built the **AI Agreement Builder** (Peter's "AI agreement processing between professionals & clients" vision) as a guided flow. Controller `app/Http/Controllers/AiAgreementBuilderController.php`, views under `resources/views/ai-agreement/build/`, routes in the shared auth group.

Flow + routes:
- **Phase 1** `ai-agreement.build` (`/ai-agreement/build`) — Discovery & AI Evidence Collection (evidence cards + confidence + missing-info detector).
- **Draft** `ai-agreement.draft` (`/ai-agreement/draft`) — generated draft where each section is tagged **🟢 AI GENERATED (auto-filled)** or **🟠 REQUIRED (user fills)** + an AI Confidence Score. This is Peter's "green = AI fill, non-green = user fills" request.
- **Phase 2** `ai-agreement.negotiate` — Collaboration & Negotiation (clauses w/ status chips + redlines, version history, comment thread, AI suggestions).
- **Phase 3** `ai-agreement.finalize` — Execution & Finalization (readiness check, e-signatures, secure archive/compliance, download PDF).

Each screen uses the role-aware `$aiLayout` pattern (supplier → `layouts.professional`, else `layouts.client`) — same trick as the [[ai-tools-role-aware-layout]] fix.

**Constraint / next step:** all evidence/clauses/signatures/sections data is **REPRESENTATIVE** (private `sample*()` methods in the controller) — NOT wired to real bookings/conversations/files yet. Peter explicitly said the green AI-fill "has to be coded". Real work remaining: populate green sections from real booking + conversation + attachments (+ Claude API/rules), real e-signature + PDF/archive backend, and an entry-point button from the booking/agreement page. Views won't need to change — just swap the sample data.

Related existing agreement feature (separate): `AgreementPageController` at `/app/agreements` (generate-from-booking + accept/reject + PDF) — the builder is the new guided front-end, not yet connected to it.


