Peter (client) laid out the AI **cost-control / abuse-prevention** architecture (relayed by Ali 2026-07-11). This is a large billable phase — flag scope before building. Ties into [[ai-iq-levels]].

**Reality check Peter is missing:** the 20 AI tools currently run on **local rule/template engines** in our own server — **zero token cost**, already no-human-intervention. Peter assumes DeepSeek is the engine; it isn't yet. So core decision = keep local (free) vs move some/all tools to **DeepSeek** (better quality, costs tokens, needs limiting) vs **hybrid** (reco: cheap tools local, premium via DeepSeek).

**Already built (~60% of Peter's limiting system):** level gating Manual/Semi/Maximum (`config/ai-levels.php` + `app/Domain/AiFeatures/AiAccess.php` + `EnsureAiLevel` middleware); per-user monthly **action cap** w/ 429 at limit (`free_beta.monthly_actions`, env `AI_FREE_BETA_MONTHLY`=60); `AiFeatureUsage` table with a **`tokens_used` column already present** (records 0 today); server-side key handling; `tool_modes` mapping 20 tools→allowed levels.

**New work Peter wants:**
1. **AI Router** abstraction (`AiRouter::complete()`) + DeepSeek driver (env key, `max_tokens`, timeout) — swappable providers, web/app code unchanged.
2. **Credit weighting** replacing flat 1/action: Light=1 (rewrite/short), Standard=2 (proposal/checklist/package desc), Advanced=4 (full event plan/contract/venue analysis), Visual=5–8 (image/portfolio/theme analysis).
3. **Plan credit grants:** Manual/Core=0, Semi/Pro-Grow=100, Maximum/Elite=400 + paid **credit packs**.
4. **Dual+ ceilings enforced simultaneously:** visible credit allowance **+ hidden monthly token budget + per-request output-token cap + rate limit** (per min/hour). First limit hit = stop.
5. **Per-tool sub-limits** (Peter's table — e.g. Event Planner 5 revisions/event, Vendor Matchmaking 10 lists, Message Assistant 100/mo at Max).
6. **Real token accounting** from DeepSeek response into `tokens_used`.
7. **User UI = "AI Assist Credits"** (never show raw tokens). Provider hidden behind name "AI Copilot" / "GigResource IQ™".
8. **Maximum AI = system-initiated actions** (software detects trigger e.g. event-date change → then calls AI for personalized output; NOT continuous polling; fixed reminders sent with no AI cost).
9. **Cost-model spreadsheet** Peter explicitly wants: per tool (avg uses/mo, avg tokens/use, monthly tokens, monthly cost, memberships) → totals per role/tier and at 100/1k/10k/100k users. He calls it the most valuable pre-launch exercise (~80–90% accurate before launch, replace w/ real data after).

**Illustrative cost/user Peter floated (NOT for pricing yet):** Client Manual $0, Client Semi $0.30–1, Client Max $1–3, Pro-Grow $2–6, Elite $5–15, Influencer $0.50–2.

**BUILT (2026-07-13) — credit metering pilot live:** `config/ai-levels.php` `credits` block (weights light1/std2/adv4/visual6, per-tool `tool_weight`, `plan_grants` starter0/professional100/enterprise400, `free_role_grant` 100). `ai_feature_usages.credits` column (migration). `AiAccess::creditsEnabled()/creditCost()/monthlyCreditGrant()`. `User::aiCreditsGrant()/aiCreditsUsedThisMonth()/aiCreditsRemaining()`. `EnsureAiLevel` meters credits (deduct per action, 429 at limit, records `credits`) when enabled, else falls back to old free-beta action cap. Visible **"AI Assist Credits"** badge = `partials/_ai_credits_badge` (in AI-tools hub). Env toggles: `AI_CREDITS_ENABLED` (default true), `AI_FREE_ROLE_CREDITS` (default 100). Verified: client grant 100 → 3×event-planner(4) = used 12/rem 88; costs correct. NOTE this is now LIVE alongside `AI_FEATURES_FREE_FOR_ALL=true` (everyone Maximum level, but metered by credits).

