All AI tools are governed by a single source of truth: **`app/Domain/AiFeatures/AiToolCatalog.php`** — every tool has `key, name, audience (client|professional|both), status (live|planned), route, purpose`. Sidebars/hub/gating read from it so the client↔pro line-up can't drift (this fixed Peter's "AI tools mixed up" complaint).

**Suites (GigResource IQ™):** the 20 tools roll up into 5 branded suites — Planning / Marketplace / Business / Operations / Automation(future). Mapping in `AiToolCatalog::SUITE_OF` + meta in `suites()`; `groupedForAudience()` returns the user's tools grouped by suite. Suites group by GOAL so they mix audiences (e.g. Marketplace = Vendor Matchmaking[client] + Staffing[pro] + Review Writer[both]). The hub renders suite-grouped. **Membership restructure DONE** (Peter/ChatGPT): `MembershipPlanSeeder` = Starter $1 / Professional $29.99 / Elite $99.99, all 6-month, suite-labelled features + 6-value framing; membership page (`dashboard/membership-plans/index.blade.php`) has the "AI by Suite" + "Opportunity Access" comparison tables. Opportunity early-access (SSR/MSR/ESR: Pro after 60 min, Elite immediate) is a **config flag** in `config/opportunities.php` — enforce when the live SSR/MSR/ESR pipeline lands. Still pending: top-level suite nav.

**Hub:** `/ai-tools` (`ai-tools.index`, `AiToolkitController`) renders each user their tools grouped by GigResource IQ™ suite, live = "Use tool", planned = "Coming soon". Role-aware via the `$aiLayout` pattern — see [[ai-tools-role-aware-layout]] (controllers set `$aiLayout = hasRole('supplier') ? 'layouts.professional' : 'layouts.client'`; views `@extends($aiLayout ?? ...)`).

**Nav + admin (added 2026-07-02):** Client & professional **sidebars are catalog-driven** — they `@foreach(AiToolCatalog::forAudience('client'|'professional'))` and render every LIVE tool (12 each: 8 role + 4 both) + an "AI Toolkit" hub link, so new tools auto-appear in nav. Layout per tool uses `$aiLayout = activeRole() === 'supplier' ? 'layouts.professional' : 'layouts.client'` (activeRole, NOT hasRole — so dual-role users see the shell for their current mode). **Admin control**: `ai_tool_settings` table (tool_key, enabled) + `Dashboard\AdminAiToolController` + `/app/ai-tools` (`app.ai-tools-admin.*`, role:admin) — admin toggles each tool; `AiToolCatalog::disabledKeys()` (memoized, try/catch-guarded) makes `forAudience()`/`groupedForAudience()` exclude disabled tools, so disabling hides them from both sidebars + the hub. Nav link in `layouts.dashboard` under `@role('admin')`.

**To build a planned tool:** create `AiXController@show` (representative data array) + `resources/views/ai-tools/<key>.blade.php` (`@extends($aiLayout)`, theme-aware vars `--bg-card/--text-primary/--border-color`) + route `/ai-tools/<key>` + flip the catalog entry `status: planned→live` and set `route`. It auto-appears in the hub.

**Status: 20 tools, ALL 20 LIVE (0 planned).** Every tool from Peter's mockups is built — the 9 dashboard tools (Event Planner, Timeline Builder, Venue Analyzer, Guest Capacity Planner, Theme & Style Advisor, Checklist Generator, Availability Optimizer, Package Builder, Portfolio Optimizer) plus the 5 input→output tools approved earlier (Bid Optimizer, Upsell Assistant [pro]; Contract Assistant, Message Assistant, Translator [both]) plus the original 6 (Budget Allocator, Vendor Matchmaking, Pricing Assistant, Proposal Writer, Staffing Planner, Review Writer).

**ALL 20 TOOLS ARE NOW FULLY FUNCTIONAL** (real input→output, verified live). ROOT CAUSE of the meeting failure: every "AI" tool called OpenAI via `SettingsService::getOpenAIKey()` which was unconfigured → "AI service unavailable" on every click. FIX = each tool now has a **deterministic local engine** (pure PHP rules/math, no API). Pattern: `<Controller>@compute(Request)` validates input → real logic → `response()->json(['success'=>true,'result'=>[...]])`; view has an id'd `<form>` + `@push('scripts')` fetch (JSON POST, `X-CSRF-TOKEN` from `meta[name=csrf-token]`, Accept json, same-origin) that renders `data.result`. Reference impl: `resources/views/client/ai-tools/budget-allocator.blade.php`.

- **6 POST tools** (Budget Allocator, Vendor Matchmaking, Review Writer had OpenAI; Pricing/Staffing/Proposal were already deterministic): the 3 OpenAI ones now do **try-AI-if-key-else-local** — `BudgetAllocatorService::allocateLocally()`, `VendorMatchmakingService::rankLocally()` (ranks REAL DB professionals!), `ReviewWriterService::composeLocally()`. If an OpenAI key is later added in Settings, they auto-upgrade to AI; without it they always return real output.
- **14 display-only tools**: each got a `compute()` method + POST route `ai-tools.<slug>.compute` (in `routes/web.php` after the GET routes) + wired form. Engines are pure rules/math (venue capacity, timeline clock-times, checklist due-dates, bid win-prob, package tiers, portfolio score, color-palette derivation, contract clauses w/ real amounts, message templates). **Translator** is the one limitation — a 29-phrase event phrasebook (5 langs); arbitrary free-text translation needs an API key.

Verified 14/14 `compute()` return `success:true` + Venue Analyzer proven live end-to-end. Tools still NOT wired to a user's own bookings/calendar/portfolio (inputs are user-entered, not auto-filled) — that's the next depth level.

**DE-AI REBRAND (2026-07-13, commit 3d796b2) — compliance, Peter+Khadijah:** Since tools run on local engines (no AI), marketing them as "AI" = false-advertising risk. **Dropped "AI" from all user-facing names/copy** (`AiToolCatalog` `name` fields + ~30 views). Rename map: Budget Allocator→**Budget Planner**, Vendor Matchmaking→**Smart Match**, Event Planner→**Guided Event Planner**, Venue Analyzer→**Venue Compatibility Check**, Checklist Generator→**Smart Checklist**, Guest Capacity Planner→**Guest Capacity Calculator**, Pricing Assistant→**Pricing Calculator**, Bid Optimizer→**Bid Calculator**, Availability Optimizer→**Availability Scheduler**, Review Writer→**Review Builder**, Message Assistant→**Message Builder**; Timeline Builder/Proposal Builder/Package Builder/Staffing Planner/Portfolio Optimizer/Upsell Assistant/Contract Assistant/Theme & Style Advisor/Translator = same minus "AI". Hub title "GigResource IQ™ — Smart Productivity Tools", `page-title` "GigResource IQ™"; sidebar section label "AI Tools"→"GigResource IQ"; suite taglines + landing copy ("AI-Powered Support"→"Guided Support", "brings more AI"→"more capability", "AI-powered booking"→"Smart booking") de-AI'd; credit badge "AI Credits"→**"IQ Credits"**. **Internal unchanged:** route names (`ai-tools.*`), catalog `key`s, controller class names (AiXController), config keys, `AiAccess`/credit logic all still use old identifiers — only labels changed. Tiers (Semi/Maximum level names) NOT yet renamed (Peter wants Manual/Assisted/Auto — separate pass). Plan: re-introduce AI later as "Now AI-enhanced" upgrade without another rename. See [[compliance-copy-rules]].


