**Done 07.26.2026.** `/browse` was largely decoration invented in the Blade; it now reads the DB.

**Replaced:**
- 6 hard-coded "trending vibes" (Unsplash + keyword guesses like `?q=wedding`) → real categories that
  **have professionals**, own artwork, live counts, filtering by `?category=` ([[pro-category-relation]]).
  **Dedupe by name** — the legacy tree repeats a service under many event types, so the raw top-6 came
  back as three copies of "DJs & Sound Services".
- Fake "Venue / Location Map" (4 pins at fixed CSS %) → **"Where they are"**: real city counts over the
  whole filtered set, each a city filter.
- "Compare Pros" card (two `href="#"` buttons) → **removed**, no such feature exists.
- "Recently Viewed" (was: first 3 search results) → real session history written by
  `ProfessionalProfileShowController::rememberView()`, newest first, hidden until non-empty.
- Card now carries the **pro's own avatar** beside the name (Freelancer's identity anchor). Hero = the
  WORK, avatar = WHO.

**TRAP 1 — portfolio column has TWO shapes.** Uploads write `['type'=>'image','hero'=>…,'square'=>…]`;
older/seeded rows hold a **bare URL string**. `portfolioImageItems()` only recognised the structured one,
so 10 of 12 pros read as having NO portfolio and every card fell to a placeholder. Now normalised, and
`portfolioHeroUrls()` passes absolute URLs through instead of handing them to `Storage::url()` (which
would emit `/storage/https://…`). Any new code reading `portfolio` must handle both.

**TRAP 2 — location counts can't GROUP BY the main query.** It carries withAvg/withCount subselects and a
HAVING on the rating alias → trips `only_full_group_by`. Materialise the filtered ids first, then count.

**TRAP 3 — `$f + ['city'=>…]` silently drops the filter.** The union operator keeps the LEFT value, and
`$f` already has an empty `'city'`. Use `array_merge`.

**Demo imagery decision (Ali, 07.26.2026):** `DemoProfessionalsSeeder` used to fill each pro's portfolio
with Unsplash URLs — 9 photos over 31 slots, one wedding bouquet on 8 of 10 pros including the DJ. Those
accounts never uploaded anything, so `'portfolio' => []` is the truth; the card falls back to the
artwork of the services they offer, and a pro with neither gets a monogram.

**ui-avatars.com is gone.** `User::getAvatarUrlAttribute()` now draws an initials SVG data URI locally
(stable hue per id); `User::placeholderAvatarUri()` covers null relations. Watch the initials builder:
words not starting with a letter/digit are skipped and the result is XML-escaped, or "Bloom & Vine Co."
yields `B&` and breaks the SVG.

