---

**Approved in the Peter ↔ Khadijah ↔ Ali thread, 2026-07-27.** Peter's final word: "Ok I agree".

**THE MODEL — settled 2026-07-27 (second message, supersedes the first).** Two *delivery mechanisms*, each
carrying a *scope*; SSR and MSR are the SCOPE, never the type:

| Type | What it is | Goes to | Scope |
|---|---|---|---|
| **BSR** — Bidding Service Request | broadcast, professionals bid | every eligible pro | SSR (single) or MSR (multi) |
| **ESR** — Emergency | *uses the BSR mechanism*, urgency flag on top | every eligible pro | SSR or MSR |
| **DSR** — Direct Service Request (was "Direct Offer") | targeted, NO bidding | one chosen pro only | SSR or MSR |

Peter's exact reasoning: "a MSRs as a stand alone would be the same as BSRs so the normal transaction would be
a single and MSRs would be a multiple transactions"; "the ESRs are actually still using the BSRs (SSRs and
MSRs) because … the client is open to every professional to get a quicker solution. They wouldn't want a DSR
(because DSRs is limited to finding a preference)"; a DSR is "not [a] bidding service request, directly
focused on the one professional of choice".

**DSR fallback:** a DSR is never offered to other professionals — *unless the client/professional deal doesn't
work out*, at which point the client may switch path or pick a different professional. That re-route is a
client action, not an automatic broadcast.

**CORRECTION — an earlier note in this file said BSR meant single-service only and MSR stayed separate. That
was wrong.** Standalone MSR *is* a BSR. Don't reintroduce that reading.

**What this means for the code:** the database model already matches — `source='user'` + published + no
`supplier_id` = BSR; `source='esr'` = ESR; `source='direct_offer'` + `supplier_id` + unpublished = DSR; scope
is the attached-category count everywhere. The work is naming/labels and the board's tab structure, not a
schema change.

**Lifecycle Peter signed off on** (he is happy with this and does not want it re-litigated):
client posts → pros are notified → pros review and bid → client reviews one or all bids → chat / negotiate →
client selects a winner. The client may edit the event description, documents etc. **until** a winner is
selected; **either side may back out until a final agreement is made**. Once a pro is selected as winner:
chat / message / create the agreement data.

**Tier access stays:** the same **60-minute** wait before Starter and Mid-level gain access. (Peter added
"I think we can remove the rest" about the other tier rules — *not decided*, he wanted Khadijah's opinion.)

**Sequencing agreed with the client** (my proposal, Khadijah restated it, Peter agreed):
1. The **8 SSR/BSR client + professional screens first** — those are what users actually touch.
2. The **Admin bidding-window settings page is its own later phase**; until it exists the bidding windows
   run on **fixed values in config**.

**Scope reality check I gave them (accepted):** this is a new build, not a revision. The new Bidding Board
and My Bids are far deeper than what is live (extra request-type tabs, saved opportunities, market insights,
table/card views, export, saved views, payout overview); the client SSR detail page becomes six tabs. The
Admin page alone (9 tabs, draft→approve→publish, versioning + rollback, threshold rule engine with overlap
detection, shared platform clock, 11-scenario test harness, 6 permissions) is bigger than the 8 screens
combined.

**Naming is SETTLED — build as BSR.** Khadijah's instruction is explicit ("designating it under a distinct
process name (Bidding Service Requests / BSRs). Please proceed with development matching these exact rules")
and Peter agreed. The mockups and R35/R37 still say SSR only because they predate the rename — they are the
screen *design*, not the naming authority. Do not re-open this; Ali confirmed 2026-07-27 that Khadijah's
wording governs.

**Open / undecided — do NOT assume:**
- **Pro → coworker sharing.** Peter wants pros to share opportunities with coworkers, "almost the same as
  freelancer website for this one area" — but explicitly said "we can go back and forth with Khadijah before
  going forward". Not in the 8 screens. Not approved.
- **"We can remove the rest"** (tier rules beyond the 60-minute window) — vague, awaiting Khadijah.

Source material lives in `~/Downloads/SSR-Professional` — 10 screen mockups + the Forms Master Inventory docx
(96 forms audited, 16 gaps still open).

