From Peter Zylstra's Developer Feedback v1.1 (June 2026) — applies to ALL user-facing copy (landing, register, dashboards, emails, plan features):

**Banned claims (legal risk — never write these):**
- Hard unverified metrics ("25,000+ professionals", "150,000+ events", "$50M+ paid", "500+ influencers", "100+ countries")
- "24/7" anything (admin is NOT available 24/7)
- "Background-checked" as a blanket claim (checks are optional, professional-paid)
- "Guaranteed" outcomes ("Success Guaranteed", "marketplace guarantee", "GigResource Guarantee")
- Blanket data-privacy promises ("your data is safe and private")
- "Expert advice / expert recommendations" and "we manage negotiations" — the platform offers neither

**Why:** Peter: "we dont give out expert advice or recommendations, nor we dont manage negotiations. Our Level of Assistance is about getting AI involved more on each level."

**How to apply:** frame assistance as **AI-powered** ("AI recommendations", "AI negotiation assistant", "AI handles the details"); use defensible value copy (escrow-protected payments, profile/business verification, privacy controls, help center). Plan-feature rows live in the `plan_features` DB table — check there too (one "Priority support 24/7" row was fixed).

**Geo-restriction (§7.1):** launch limited to MD, VA, DC, DE, PA, NJ, NY. `config/geo.php` holds `allowed_states` + a 3-digit `zip_prefixes` map (built with `array_replace`, NOT spread — spread renumbers integer keys). Registration: professionals = hardcoded state dropdown; clients = zip validation.

**Address verification + geolocation (§7.2–7.5) — SCAFFOLD DONE (don't rebuild):** `app/Domain/AddressVerification/` (AddressStatus labels, AddressFilter=Layer-1 free PO Box/blank/junk filter [REAL, no API], AddressVerificationGuard=paid-API go-live lock, providers USPS/Google=stubs awaiting keys, AddressVerificationService=risk-based state machine attempts→lockout) + `app/Domain/Geolocation/GeolocationService.php` (session [wired in RegisterController] + Cloudflare CF-Region headers = REAL; HTML5 + MaxMind = stubs). Config `config/address_verification.php`. DB: `user_profiles.address_status` + attempts/flagged_home/verified_at/locked_at/meta (migration 2026_06_18_000001). UI: professional profile General tab → "Business Address Verification" card + `professional.profile.verify-address` POST. Clients = frictionless (full addr only at booking, `PRIVATE_CLIENT_HIDDEN`). Doc: `docs/address-verification.md`. **LAUNCH SWITCH `ADDRESS_VERIFICATION_GO_LIVE`** (`.env`, default false): pre-launch NO paid call — filter-passing addrs → "Manual Review Required", 0 attempts spent. At launch: provision USPS/Google account, implement provider `verify()` (TODO markers), set flag=true + `ADDRESS_VERIFICATION_DRIVER`/key + `config:clear`. Another dormant go-live flag alongside [[production-hosting]] payments lock + the AI_FEATURES flag above.

**DMCA (§1.3):** `/dmca-policy` (PolicyPage slug `dmca-policy`) + notice form → `dmca_reports` table; uploads require rights confirm() and are logged ("Image upload (rights confirmed)").

**Platform disclaimer (§1.2) — DONE (June 2026):** the banned-claim limitations are now positively surfaced, so don't re-build this. (a) Onboarding notice partial `partials/_onboarding_disclaimer.blade.php` included in BOTH register forms (above submit). (b) Dedicated page `/platform-disclaimer` (route name `platform-disclaimer`) renders `policies.show`; content seeded by `PlatformDisclaimerSeeder` (idempotent `updateOrCreate`, registered in DatabaseSeeder; PolicyPage slug `platform-disclaimer`). Linked in both footers (landing bottom-bar + dark `partials/footer.blade.php` Policies col).

**Notification prefs (§3.1) — DONE:** moved off the profile tab into dedicated pages — `client.notifications.index` (`/client/notifications`, orange) + `professional.notifications.index` (`/professional/notifications`, blue); views in `resources/views/{client,professional}/notifications/index.blade.php`, post to existing `*.profile.update.notifications` PATCH. Profile "Notifications" tab + priority-page "Go to Notification Settings" link repoint here; in-profile notification blocks removed. Admin profile still uses the old inline tab (out of v1.1 scope).

**Button style guide (§4.2) — DONE:** `docs/button-style-guide.md` — role colour fixed (client=orange `--accent-orange #f97316`, professional=blue `--accent-blue #2563eb`), size varies; variants + existing-class map + checklist. No global `.btn` added (collides with existing per-component classes).

**AI tools by tier (§8.3) — DONE:** infra already existed (`app/Domain/AiFeatures/` — AiFeatureCode, AiFeatureGate, `User::aiFeatureAccess`, `ai_feature_usages`); was un-seeded + 2 controllers ungated. Fixed: AI entitlements now seeded as structured rows inside `MembershipPlanSeeder` (each plan's `features[]` accepts `['feature'=>…,'feature_code'=>'ai.x','quota_monthly'=>N]`; loop handles string|array). Matrix: Review Writer = Starter 10/mo, Pro/Ent unlimited; Budget Allocator + Vendor Matchmaking = Pro/Ent only (30/mo / unlimited), locked on Starter. Wired AiFeatureGate authorize+recordUsage+status into AiVendorMatchmakingController + AiReviewWriterController (Budget Allocator already did). Shared badge `partials/_ai_quota_badge.blade.php`. Deterministic tools (Pricing/Proposal/Staffing) stay free (no LLM). Doc: `docs/ai-tools-by-tier.md`. Also fixed latent banned claim in seeder: Enterprise "Priority support 24/7" → "Priority support".

**LAUNCH SWITCH — `AI_FEATURES_FREE_FOR_ALL`:** `.env` currently `true` → ALL users get unlimited AI regardless of plan (`User::aiFeatureAccess` short-circuits). Gating is wired but DORMANT (like the payments go-live lock). At launch: set `=false` (already false in `.env.example`) + `php artisan config:clear`, together with membership/Stripe go-live — else demo accounts w/o subscription get locked out. Admins always bypass.

