## memory/legacy-categories-import.md

---
name: legacy-categories-import
description: "How the 360 event categories (4-level tree + images) were imported from the old GigResource site into khadija-project, and how to refresh them."
metadata: 
  node_type: memory
  type: project
  originSessionId: 85789cbb-33fa-475d-a481-c0a769b18371
---

The new project's event-category taxonomy is the **exact live tree from the old GigResource site** (hosted at `bingo-agency.com/gigresource.com`). Peter wants these categories at all costs; everything else deleted.

**Source of truth = the LIVE site, not any local dump.** The local `gigresource.sql` (Dec) and `~/Downloads/gigresso_platform.sql` (Jun 13) were BOTH stale — only 175 categories, 3 levels. The live DB had grown to **360 categories, 49 roots, 4 levels deep** (ids up to 600+). Restructured after June.

**Pull current live data via the public API** (no auth, CORS open):
`https://bingo-agency.com/gigresource.com/adminlab/upload/<file>` for images, and the category list from:
`https://bingo-agency.com/gigresource.com/adminlab/api/fetchAllCategories.php` (returns all categories as JSON, `parent_id` = tree; `image`/`cover_image` = filenames in `adminlab/upload/`).

**Import pipeline → permanent seeder:**
- `database/seeders/CategorySeeder.php` — wipes categories (FK-safe: clears `category_event` + nulls `events.category_id`), then 2-pass insert (all rows first, then remap `parent_id` via old→new id map — handles any depth). `sort_order = old_id` so admin can show "newest first". Registered in `DatabaseSeeder`.
- `database/seeders/data/legacy_categories.json` (360 rows) + `database/seeders/assets/categories/` (~130MB, 360 images) ship with the repo so reinstall reproduces it.
- Admin ordering matches legacy: cards `orderByDesc('sort_order')` (newest first), tree `orderBy('name')` (alphabetical, recursive/infinite via `_tree_item.blade.php` + `Category::allChildren`).
- Card image uses `cover_image ?: thumbnail` (most legacy rows only have `image`→thumbnail).

**To refresh again:** re-fetch the API JSON, download images (parallel curl), regenerate the JSON + assets, `php artisan db:seed --class=CategorySeeder`.

Note: live data has genuine duplicate titles (e.g. "Livestock Shows & Animal Handlers" ×2, "Unique Themes" ×4) — kept faithful; Ali may later ask to dedupe. See [[peter-requirements-backlog]].


