---

**Built 07.26.2026.** Before this there was NO link between professionals and categories — only
`category_event` (categories ↔ events). Discovery guessed with `LIKE '%<full category name>%'` against
the pro's free-text `headline`/`bio`/`skills`, which matched nothing ("Fine-Art Wedding Photographer"
never contains "Photography Services"). Result: all 360 category landing pages showed **0 pros**, and
the "Browse all <category>" button passed `/browse` the same doomed `?q=`.

**What exists now:**
- `category_user` pivot · `User::serviceCategories()` · `Category::professionals()`
- Professional profile → Professional tab → **"Services You Offer"** card (`<x-service-picker>`, blue
  accent), route `professional.profile.update.services` (PATCH).
- `/browse?category=<slug>` — real relation filter, matches the category **and every descendant**, so a
  group page returns the specialists under it. Category landing pages link with this, not `?q=`.
- `DemoProfessionalsSeeder` has a `'services' => [names…]` key per pro and an `attachServices()` helper.

**THE TRAP — read before touching the save:** the legacy tree repeats the same service name under many
event types ("Event Photography" exists a dozen times). `<x-service-picker>` dedupes by NAME, so the
form can only ever submit ONE id per name. Syncing those ids verbatim drops the pro from every other
branch — the first save cut Duy Nguyen from 21 pivot rows to 6. `updateServices()` therefore expands the
picked ids → names → **all** ids with those names before `sync()`. Same reason the seeder matches on
name. Any new surface that writes `category_user` must do the same expansion.

**Also fixed on the landing page (same pass):** `4.8★ Avg rating` and `24h Avg quote time` were
hard-coded literals in the Blade — invented platform data and a banned claim per
[[compliance-copy-rules]]. Removed. The pro count is real but now renders only when > 0 ("0+ Pros
