The public-facing marketing site (GigResource) is being redesigned from the old **dark** theme to a **light** theme matching the client mockups (white bg, navy text, blue #2563eb + orange #f97316 accents — same palette as the dashboards).

**Architecture decision (2026-06-11):** The homepage was rebuilt against a NEW self-contained light layout `resources/views/layouts/landing.blade.php` (its own light navbar + footer + inline-SVG hexagon logo, real routes + @auth/@guest states). The view `resources/views/landing.blade.php` (`@extends('layouts.landing')`, `lp-` prefixed classes) holds all reference sections: hero w/ floating cards, 5-col trust bar, categories carousel, 5-step How-It-Works, 3 assistance cards, why-choose + video + testimonial, gradient metrics bar, pricing, CTA banner.

**MIGRATION COMPLETE (2026-07-23).** Every view is off the dark layout — `grep -rn "layouts\.public"` over `resources/views/` + `app/` returns nothing. `layouts/public.blade.php` and `partials/_public_styles.blade.php` are dead code, left on disk. The last pages converted were `errors/_layout`, `public/professional/show`, `policies/show`, `blog/show`. **Peter rejects any dark public page on sight — if one reappears, convert it, don't ship it.**

**Two traps when converting a page to `layouts.landing`:**
1. *Hero over a photo* — convert line-aware. Rules for the hero block keep explicit `rgba(255,255,255,…)` / `#fff`; only the body region moves to light tokens. Blanket search-replace turns hero text white-on-white.
2. *Scrim gradients silently vanish.* `linear-gradient(… , var(--bg-dark) 100%)` — `--bg-dark` doesn't exist in the light layout, and one invalid stop makes the browser drop the **entire** gradient, washing out the hero title. End the gradient on an explicit `rgba(11,15,26,0.86)`.

Also: the landing header is **in flow**, not fixed — old pages carry `padding-top: 180px` (mobile 140px) to clear the old fixed navbar. Cut it to ~72px / 48px or the page opens on a band of blank white.

Same class of bug inside the dashboards: `layouts/professional.blade.php` defines `--text-primary` / `--text-secondary` / `--text-muted` / `--border-color`, but **not** `--text-white` or `--text-light`. Views using the latter fell back to inherited colour. Use the pro tokens — they flip with that layout's own light/dark toggle.

Real/dynamic data on the homepage: `LandingPageController` provides `$plans` (MembershipPlan + features → pricing cards), `$metrics` (real aggregates w/ marketing floor), `$featuredReview` (testimonial fallback to illustrative). Category tiles + hero "Top Match" card are curated/illustrative because the live Category table is junk test rows and there are 0 reviews / no review-backed top pro.

**Auth pages redesign (2026-06-19):** register + login rebuilt to the new light two-column mockups via a shared `resources/views/layouts/auth-pro.blade.php` (`apx-` prefixed classes). Role-themed by a `@php` map keyed on `@section('apRole', …)`: **client/affiliate/login = orange #f97316, professional = blue #2563eb**. Left panel = "Join Event Pro Marketplace" + role tagline + 4 benefits + trust band (Trusted by Global Brands / Fast Campaign Launches / Secure Payments / Real-Time Analytics); right = form card with **placeholder** Google/Apple OAuth buttons (no Socialite backend — "Soon" badge). Pages: `auth/register.blade.php` (role-driven client|supplier via `?role=`, geo zip/state PRESERVED, onboarding disclaimer kept), `auth/login.blade.php`, `influencer/join.blade.php` (affiliate — kept its real *application* fields: full_name/email/social/audience/reach, NOT a password account). RegisterController now also validates `phone` (nullable → saved to user) + `agree` (ToS, accepted). **Four SEPARATE login pages** (per audience, all post to the one `Auth::routes()` POST `/login` handler — auth is role-agnostic, only the look differs):
- `/login` → **Client** (orange) — default; `auth/login.blade.php` reads `$loginRole` (default 'client').
- `/professional/login` (route `login.professional`) → **Professional** (blue) — renders `auth.login` with `loginRole='supplier'`.
- `/affiliate/login` (route `login.affiliate`) → **Affiliate** (orange) — `loginRole='influencer'`.
- `/admin/login` (route `admin.login`) → **Admin** — separate view `auth/admin-login.blade.php`, clean dark-navy "Admin Portal" card (no marketing/OAuth, NO fake metrics).
All three user logins share `auth/login.blade.php` (themed via `$loginRole` → heading "Professional/Affiliate Sign In", matching register link, cross-links). The `/professional/login` & `/affiliate/login` GET routes + `/admin/login` sit right after `Auth::routes();` in web.php, all `guest` middleware.

