---

Peter delivered the **full platform workflow set** (~48 workflows, 6 categories) as the canonical spec, reconciled/dated **2026-07-15** (earlier versions had version-drift — older docs weren't updated as new ones were added; the 07.15 set is authoritative). Source docs are Claude-generated reviews Peter runs against a [LEGAL] counsel-reviewed policy set + [FLOW] flowchart + [YOU] chat statements. **These reviews are high-quality and mostly accurate** — I verified key claims against code.

## THE BIG FINDING (highest-priority build)
**`/client/post-event` is a package SHOPPING/ordering wizard (synchronous → ends at Checkout), NOT a posting-and-bidding flow.** 7 of its 10 steps are package ops (Results → Compare → Customize → Combinations → Checkout). No posting is created, no pro ever responds. Peter's instinct was right.
**Fix (no new UI — re-scope existing screens):**
1. Add **Step 1 "Choose Route"**: SSR · MSR · ESR · Direct Offer · Package Search. Packages become ONE route of five, not the whole product.
2. Posting routes (SSR/MSR/ESR) **end at "Publish"** — then bids arrive asynchronously on **`/client/proposals`** (this async surface is "the missing half" — page exists but isn't wired to a posting→bid loop).
3. **Bidding Board (`/professional/bidding-board`) is already built & correct** — just needs MSR/ESR listings + bid form + net-commission shown, fed from published postings.
4. Keep package steps 5–10, scoped to Package route only. Nothing is deleted — the package flow is real, just mis-scoped.

## Core architecture (confirmed correct in code — do NOT redo)
- **Per-service = separate gig**: each requested service is awarded, contracted, and paid separately. MSR review findings #24–28 confirm this is built right and consistent.
- **MSR and ESR use the SAME per-service bidding model** — whatever is built for MSR bids serves ESR.
- **Direct Offer = NON-bidding**: targeted invite to specific pro(s); pro Accept/Decline/Reply. Same service → one pro at a time (sequential re-offer if declined); different services → different pros in parallel. Partial-fill: accepted services lock, unfilled stay OPEN → client re-routes remainder via the same 5-route chooser (2nd Direct Offer / MSR / ESR / Package). See [[request-types-esr]].
- **Universal counter loop**: Accept / Decline / **Reply** everywhere (unlimited back-and-forth until deal/no-deal). Several screens show only Accept/Decline — **Reply button missing** (My Proposals, ESR response) — must add.

## Confirmed fee schedule ([LEGAL])
Posting: **$2.99** per post (regardless of outcome). Service fee: **$4.99** per finalized SSR/MSR-gig/Direct Offer; **$8.99** ESR — charged ONLY on finalized agreement, "never on deals that fall through." **$4.99** one-time ID verification (+18+ +ToS/Privacy/E-Sign = preconditions to post). Commission Starter 5% / Pro 3% / Elite 1.5% (professional-absorbed, deducted by processor at payout). See [[peter-requirements-backlog]] pricing.

## PROGRESS (2026-07-16, Ali greenlit)
- **Phase 1 DONE + committed:** geo NY→WV (`72468c7`), Team/Co-Op removal (`2258551`,`4cf81bf`), RFP→MSR (`a8f8da2`). See [[team-mode-removal]].
- **Phase 2 keystone DONE (`7d17734`):** `/client/post-event` now opens on a **Choose Route** step (`client.post-event.choose`) — Shop Packages / MSR / Direct Offer (live) + SSR / ESR ("Coming soon"). All "Post an Event" entry points repointed to it; package wizard is now just the Package Search route. Verified rendered as client@example.com.
- **Phase 2 core loop LIVE + verified end-to-end (`51f8fcd`, `2c4682d`):** MSR "Publish Request" (`ClientMultiServiceController::store`) creates a real published `Event` (services = categories) → surfaces on the pro **Bidding Board** (already queries published events) → pro `placeBid` (sealed-bids, exists) → **client `/client/proposals` now sourced from `Bid`** shows the incoming bid with real amount/status/pipeline. Proven: Event #85 + $4,200 bid visible on Proposals.
- **Phase 2 loop EXTENDED (07.16, all verified):** net-commission preview on pro bid form (`b82c012`); client **Accept/Decline award** on Proposals (`ca6a0a1`); pro **award status** "You won/Not selected" on My Bids (`a370b53`); **Reply/counter-offer negotiation** both sides via `bid_replies` table + shared `_bid-thread` partial (`029cdac`). Full loop now: post→publish→bid(net)→proposals→Accept/Decline/Reply→award visible both sides.
- **Award→Booking + Direct Offer wired (07.16, verified):** accepting a bid creates a confirmed `Booking` (price=bid amount, source 'bid') shown on client Bookings (`43bb35e`, also fixed a pre-existing 500 there — escrow sweep had broken the `locked_escrow` array key). Direct Offer builder now submits (`2d21b6f`): creates a targeted Event (supplier_id set, is_published=FALSE so NOT on open board, source 'direct_offer').
- **Direct Offer loop COMPLETE both sides (`c39d0fc`):** pro Direct Offer page loads the real targeted offer + Accept (→ confirmed Booking) / Decline. Full DO chain works: client sends → pro sees real offer → responds → booking.
- **Remaining Phase 2 (NOT done):** funding/Payment-Secured status on Booking (gateway deferred); **per-service MSR rows** on Bidding Board (bids are per-event not per-service — needs a category_id on bids, a schema change); SSR + ESR client flows (route chooser shows them "coming soon"); ESR pages both sides.
- **FULL LIFECYCLE FUNCTIONAL (07.16, verified end-to-end):** post → bid(net commission) → Proposals → Accept/Decline/Reply(counter) → award → confirmed Booking → pro **Mark Delivered** (completed) → client **Review** (5★). Plus Direct Offer both sides. Commits `2b69816` (mark delivered) + `6dd70d5` (review). Deploy is Ali's responsibility (he confirmed).
